  "name": "Motrebi and ruhowzi (Tehran entertainers' song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Light popular music of the motrebs, professional entertainers who played at weddings, feasts and private parties in Qajar and Pahlavi Tehran, and of ruhowzi, the improvised comic theatre staged on boards laid over a courtyard pool, in which songs, dances and comic routines alternated. Its witty, often bawdy songs in Tehrani dialect use the lighter modes of Persian music, with tombak and dayereh rhythms under voice, tar or violin.",
